  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Ligand which has two different donor atoms and either of the two donor atom is attached to the metal during complex formation is called ambidentate ligand. Among the given ligands&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>NCS</mi><mo>-</mo></msup><mfenced><msup><mi>SCN</mi><mo>-</mo></msup></mfenced><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>and</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msubsup><mi>NO</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo></msubsup><mfenced><msup><mi>ONO</mi><mo>-</mo></msup></mfenced></math>&nbsp;are&nbsp; ambidentate ligands</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msubsup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>4</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>&#160;</mo><mfenced><mi>bidentate</mi></mfenced></math>,ethylenediamine(bidentate) and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></math>(monodentate)&nbsp;ligands are not ambidentate.</p>",
